{
  "tema": 5059,
  "slug": "querer-que-subjuntivo",
  "titulo": "Querer que + the present subjunctive",
  "subtitulo": "Quiero que vengas: when you want someone else to do something.",
  "foto": "t04.jpg",
  "regla": "Querer que + present subjunctive when the subjects are different; same subject: querer + infinitive.",
  "comparada_kwiziq": "2026-10-10",
  "secciones": [
    {
      "id": "regla",
      "titulo": "The rule",
      "bloques": [
        {
          "tipo": "texto",
          "texto": "To say _to want someone to do something_, use **querer que** + the **present subjunctive**. This is always true, also in negative sentences and in questions."
        },
        {
          "tipo": "formula",
          "partes": [
            "**querer**",
            "**que**",
            "present subjunctive"
          ]
        },
        {
          "tipo": "texto",
          "texto": "This happens because there are **two different subjects**: one person wants, and another person does. In **mis amigos quieren que sea más sociable**, the subject of **querer** is **mis amigos**, and the subject of **ser** is **yo**."
        },
        {
          "tipo": "texto",
          "texto": "If the subject is **the same** for both verbs, drop **que** and use the **infinitive**: **quiero salir** (I want, I go out)."
        },
        {
          "tipo": "tabla",
          "encabezados": [
            "Subjects",
            "Structure",
            "Example"
          ],
          "filas": [
            [
              "different",
              "querer que + subjunctive",
              "Quiero que salgas."
            ],
            [
              "the same",
              "querer + infinitive",
              "Quiero salir."
            ]
          ]
        },
        {
          "tipo": "texto",
          "texto": "The same goes for **desear**, a stronger synonym of **querer**: **deseo que seas feliz**, but **deseo enviar un mensaje**."
        },
        {
          "tipo": "texto",
          "texto": "Tip: one person, one verb in infinitive. Two people, **que** builds a bridge and the subjunctive crosses it."
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "ejemplos",
      "titulo": "Examples",
      "bloques": [
        {
          "tipo": "ejemplos",
          "lista": [
            {
              "es": "No quiero que me ==llames== tan temprano.",
              "en": "I don't want you to call me so early."
            },
            {
              "es": "¿Qué quieres que ==haga==?",
              "en": "What do you want me to do?"
            },
            {
              "es": "Mi mamá quiere que ==estudie== más.",
              "en": "My mom wants me to study more."
            },
            {
              "es": "Todos queremos que el problema ==se resuelva== pronto.",
              "en": "We all want the problem to be solved soon."
            },
            {
              "es": "¿Quieren que los ==lleve== a la playa?",
              "en": "Do you want me to take you to the beach?"
            },
            {
              "es": "Tus amigos quieren que ==seas== más sociable.",
              "en": "Your friends want you to be more sociable."
            },
            {
              "es": "Quiero ==entrenar== hoy en la noche.",
              "en": "I want to train tonight. (same subject)"
            },
            {
              "es": "Deseo que ==tengan== unas buenas vacaciones.",
              "en": "I hope you have a good vacation."
            }
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "trampa",
      "titulo": "The trap",
      "bloques": [
        {
          "tipo": "pares",
          "lista": [
            {
              "filas": [
                {
                  "v": "mal",
                  "t": "Quiero que tú vienes."
                },
                {
                  "v": "bien",
                  "t": "Quiero que tú vengas."
                }
              ],
              "nota": "After **querer que**, never the ordinary present."
            },
            {
              "filas": [
                {
                  "v": "mal",
                  "t": "Quiero que yo salga temprano."
                },
                {
                  "v": "bien",
                  "t": "Quiero salir temprano."
                }
              ],
              "nota": "Same subject: infinitive, no **que**."
            },
            {
              "filas": [
                {
                  "v": "mal",
                  "t": "Beto quiere tú lo ayudes."
                },
                {
                  "v": "bien",
                  "t": "Beto quiere que lo ayudes."
                }
              ],
              "nota": "The **que** is never dropped when the subjects differ."
            }
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
